module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "diagnostic name accurate about the situation, silent about the mechanism (a diagnostic's NAME describes the state it was raised in faithfully and says nothing about WHICH PREDICATE produced it, so a reader who treats the name as a cause builds a coherent story with no load-bearing contact with the code. ",

    "Nothing in the name is wrong, which is why review reads past it. ",

    "THREE RECEIPTS IN ONE NIGHT FROM THREE READERS, provenance stated per receipt because a row about untraced names must not itself rest on an untraced relay. ",

    "FIRST, measured by this row's author, and it leads because the reader was the author of the story: rustc labels reading `expected Rc<Vector<i64>>, found String` at 49 sites plus 2 reversed, from which a representation fork was inferred -- the model type `Symbol` rendering as `String` in parameter position and a vector in field position -- and published. ",

    "Measured: `Symbol` renders CONSISTENTLY as `String`, `Connective.Atom` carries `identity: String`, and the `.dag` is well-typed with the same declared type on both sides. ",

    "The published mechanism was wrong; the label was a faithful description of a mismatch the type-checker had computed. ",

    "AND THE CHECK FAILED THE SAME WAY THE READING DID, which is the most instructive part rather than decoration: a grep for the printed type name returned zero and zero was read as absence, when the emitted source spells `Rc<Vec<i64>>` and `lib.rs` carries `use im::Vector as Vec`, so rustc was printing the resolved underlying name. ",

    "A name was read as a fact about the tree twice in one investigation, once in the diagnostic and once in the refutation of it. ",

    "WHAT THE 49 SITES ACTUALLY ARE, and it is UNCHASED: `Rc<Vec<i64>>` is how `List<Int>` renders, so they read expected `List<Int>` found `String` -- an ordinary mechanism, and a real one. ",

    "The amendment closed the wrong explanation, not the defect. ",

    "SECOND, reported by quick-bat-372 and independently verified: `MethodNotFound` names the situation correctly and does not say which predicate gates it -- `method_existence_decision` gates on `kernel_profile_lookup`, so a fully resolved USER product with no kernel profile answers `MethodExistenceUndecided`. ",

    "THIRD, same provenance: `FieldNotFound` names a concept never emitted for field ACCESS at all, established by exhausting its three construction sites -- two pattern bindings and one guarded by a record literal's field names. ",

    "WHY IT EARNS A ROW: two of the three would have shipped as PERMANENTLY-GREEN WITNESS ARMS, an assertion that a wall fired over a wall that cannot fire for that input, which is section 4b's decoration-cited-as-coverage reached by a route no other row names -- and all three were caught by reading the PRODUCER rather than by review. ",

    "WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: three instances in one night is a suggestive rate and not a base rate; all three surfaced while several lanes were unusually deep in diagnostic populations, so the frequency is a property of that work rather than of the corpus. ",

    "Recognition rule: before treating a diagnostic name as a mechanism, read the function that produces it and find the predicate that gates it; if you cannot name that predicate, you have a situation and not a cause. ",

    "A grep for the type name is a cheap first pass, not a sufficient check: rustc prints resolved names while source spells aliases, so `use X as Y` defeats the search in both directions and a zero can be confident and wrong. ",

    "Read the producer. ",

    "AMENDED 2026-08-28 -- THE PRODUCER'S OWN PROSE IS ALSO A NAME, so `read the producer` is necessary and NOT SUFFICIENT. ",

    "The three receipts above are all DIAGNOSTIC names; the same failure reaches COMMENTS, and it is harder to see there because a comment is where a reader goes to ESCAPE the name. ",

    "Two variants, and the ranking is the whole point. ",

    "STALE prose is FALSIFIABLE BY READING: what it says is contradicted by the code as it stands, so a reader who checks the producer can always catch it. ",

    "THAT IS NOT THE SAME AS SELF-CORRECTING, and an earlier revision of this row said it was -- `it rots when the code moves, and whoever next touches that code notices` -- which THIS ROW'S OWN SECOND RECEIPT REFUTES (review 57329): the deleted/still-here contradiction is LIVE in the tree today, and it was found by a reader who had gone there for an unrelated reason, NOT by the next person to touch the code. ",

    "So the ranking below is about FALSIFIABILITY and not about correction rate. ",

    "Stale prose persists exactly as long as nobody reads it, which is indefinitely; what makes it the lesser of the two is that a reader who does check is guaranteed to see the disagreement. ",

    "WRONG-MECHANISM-CORRECT-CONCLUSION is NOT self-limiting: nothing it says is falsified by moving the code, so it survives every refactor, and the defect it names really existing READS AS CONFIRMATION of the explanation it gives -- load-bearing misinformation with a correct headline, routing every future reader to the wrong repair. ",

    "RECEIPT, read independently by three readers rather than relayed: the comment above the floor's live-tree scan says its two computations `cannot agree except by coincidence` because one is a syntactic scan and the other falls through to `effect_reach_derived_reads_live_tree_for_entry`, a SEMANTIC reachability derivation -- locating the cause in the import graph. ",

    "Read the control flow: `reads_live_tree_effective` calls `parse_entry_live_tree_disposition` first, and an UNDECLARED file reaches `Ok(declared.unwrap_or(true))`, so the function RETURNS before the derivation is consulted. ",

    "The largest and simplest disagreement class is decided before the import graph is reached, and the mechanism the comment names has nothing to do with it. ",

    "A SECOND RECEIPT FROM THE SAME PARAGRAPH, in the stale variant: it states the floor's copy is DELETED rather than reconciled, in the past tense, four lines above a section headed WHY IT IS STILL HERE explaining that the scan is live. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, extending the one above rather than replacing it: THE CODE PATH IS THE FACT, and every sentence around it -- in a note, in a doc, or in the producer's own comment -- is commentary that may be stale or may be wrong about WHY. ",

    "And having reached the producer, do not stop at the sentence that confirms your framing: this amendment exists because a reader quoted IT IS NO WALL from such a comment and dropped `and it is a partial classifier, not an enforcement` from four lines below, inside the same citation.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
